@@ -15,3 +15,36 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Passkeys and account settings
+
+Sign-in offers both passkeys (including browser autofill) and passwords. Sign-up
+creates a password account, signs in, and offers optional passkey enrollment.
+Account settings at `/devtools-times/account/settings` lets signed-in readers
+add, rename, or delete passkeys and change their display name. Each change asks
+for passkey reauthentication or the existing password. Username changes remain
+owned by the external password service.
+
+Password registration and verification still use the existing remote Times API.
+Passwords and upstream tokens are never stored locally. Local sessions use an
+HttpOnly, SameSite cookie; the server verifies passkeys with SimpleWebAuthn,
+including their origin, RP ID, one-use session challenge, account ownership,
+user verification, and signature counter. AAGUID provider names/icons are display
+hints only, from a small local snapshot of the
+[passkey provider registry](https://github.com/passkeydeveloper/passkey-authenticator-aaguids).
+Unrecognized authenticators use a generic icon.
+
+Configure the runtime environment using `.env.example`. `AUTH_ORIGIN` must match
+the URL readers actually use, including the port in local development;
+`AUTH_RP_ID` is its domain without a port. Production defaults match the canonical
+site in `astro.config.mjs`. Localhost permits WebAuthn over HTTP; other origins
+require HTTPS. Passkeys are tied to the RP ID, so changing domains requires new
+registration. Keep this configuration stable.
+
+`AUTH_STORE_PATH` defaults to `.data/auth.json`. This sample stores public keys,
+credential metadata, account links, hashed session tokens, and expiring challenges
+in an atomically written private file. **Run a single Node process with a durable
+private volume.** For multiple instances, replace `withAuthStore` with a shared
+transactional database before deploying. Losing this file loses passkeys; the
+existing remote password login remains the recovery method. Sessions expire
+after 12 hours; challenges and recent identity verification expire after 5 minutes.
